# --- Never commit: the local data directory ---------------------------------
# `/data` is the local app's data directory — the laptop's echo of the volume
# the deployed instance mounts. It holds the card pool, the Scryfall bulk
# files it is built from, the caches, and `app.db`, and none of it is
# repository content: the pool is re-downloadable in one command and
# redistributing their files is against Scryfall's guidelines (ADR 6), while
# `app.db` is the other half of ADR 4 — users, password hashes, and since
# ADR 16 email addresses. It is the one file here that is irreplaceable and
# the one that must never be public.
#
# **Leading slash, and it is load-bearing** — the same trap `/decks/` documents
# below. Bare `data/` matches a directory of that name at *any* depth, and four
# packages ship an embedded `data/` of checked-in JSON (`internal/reference`,
# `internal/tarot`, `internal/claude` and its `tools`). Anchored, this matches
# only the app's data directory, which is all this paragraph ever claimed.
#
# Nothing here is tracked, not even a `.gitkeep`: the code that needs the
# directory makes it (`os.MkdirAll` in the pool's refresh and the auth
# schema), so an empty placeholder bought nothing and read as though the
# directory were repository content.
/data/

# The WAL siblings at any depth, deliberately unanchored: a `-wal` alone can
# contain committed rows, and a stray handle can open one outside `/data`.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Backups pulled off a deployed instance (docs/HOSTING.md §5). An `app.db`
# backup is an `app.db` — password hashes and email addresses — and the deck
# copies alongside it are somebody else's writing. The filename check in CI
# catches `app.db` by name; this keeps the whole directory out by intent.
backups/

# --- Never commit: Forge's distribution, its card data, or a JVM ------------
# Tier 3 keeps all of this outside the repository on purpose (see
# `config.forge_home`), so these patterns should never match anything. They are
# here for the day somebody unpacks the tarball in the working directory:
# `res/cardsfolder` is a second engine's card pool and rule 5 covers it, the
# jar is 40 MB of binary, and a `.dck` is generated input to a simulator rather
# than one of the five artifacts.
forge/
forge-*.jar
jdk-*/
*.dck

# --- Never commit: decks -----------------------------------------------------
# Decks are live app data, not repository content (ADR 30). `decks/` is the
# local app's data directory — every editing route writes it, `decks delete`
# moves a deck into `decks/.trash/` inside it — and the deployed copy lives on
# the volume at /data/decks. Tracking it meant two diverging copies and a
# working tree the app dirtied by being used. `deck.yaml` is still the source
# of truth; git is just not where it lives.
#
# **Leading slash, and it is load-bearing.** Bare `decks/` matches a directory
# of that name at *any* depth, so it also swallowed `src/mtglab/decks/` — the
# deck source package, thirteen modules. Those stayed tracked (an ignore rule
# cannot untrack a tracked file), so nothing broke and nothing said anything;
# what it cost was the *next* module, which `git add` would have refused and
# `git add -A` would have skipped in silence. Anchored, this matches only the
# app's data directory, which is all the paragraph above ever claimed.
/decks/

# --- Never commit: anything that identifies what you physically own ---------
# A public inventory of expensive cards tied to a real identity is a
# targeting list. Keep these local, permanently.
collection.yaml
collection/
wishlist.yaml
**/inventory.*
**/purchases.*
**/orders.*

# --- Never commit: credentials and sessions ---------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# ...except the template, which carries names and no values. The negation has
# to come after `.env.*` or it is overridden rather than overriding.
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
cookies.json
**/session*.json
.credentials/

# --- Frontend ---------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules is huge and reproducible from package-lock.json.
node_modules/
web/dist/
.vite/

# NOTE: web_dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the built app,
# and committing it is what lets someone clone this repo and run `mtglab ui`
# without installing Node at all. Rebuild it with `npm --prefix web run build`.

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Hypothesis's example database: a local cache of previously-failing inputs so
# they get replayed first. Machine-specific, and CI runs with database=None.
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# --- OS / editor ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# The Go binary, wherever a local build drops it. Two paths, and the second
# is the one that mattered: `go build ./cmd/mtglab` with no `-o` leaves an
# 89MB Mach-O next to `go.mod`, and CLAUDE.md's own Setup block says
# `go build -o ../mtglab ./cmd/mtglab`, which leaves the same 89MB at the
# repository root. Only the first was covered, so the net missed the case the
# documentation actually tells people to run. The image builds to `/out` and
# CI to a temp path; neither is ever in a working tree.
go/mtglab
/mtglab

# The scribe compiles to class files; the sources are the artifact.
scribe/out/
